Rule 1 (start_dim and end_dim must be valid dimension indices for the input tensor)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= 0 - ndim(v_3) ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ ndim(v_3) - 1 ∧ 0 - ndim(v_3) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_3) - 1
>>
Rule 2 (start_dim cannot come after end_dim)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 ≤ v_2
>>
Rule 3 (with default parameters, input must be at least 2-D)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= if (v_1 = 1 ∧ v_2 = -1) then ndim(v_3) ≥ 2
